 "summary": "Organizations can now invite people. A Product invites an email with a role, gets a one-time token, and later accepts it for a signed-in user.",
 "verdict": {
  "risk": "medium",
  "door": "two-way",
  "ask": "Status is computed rather than stored, a row lock keeps one pending invitation per email, and the token alone is enough to join.",
  "doorNote": "Additive only. The down migration drops the table."
 },
